  "question": "Can the 2010 《文津学志》第三辑 containing 《〈冀淑英文集〉补遣》 be bound to exact institutional physical holdings for lawful direct collation, and do the public OPAC routes currently expose article-level pages or text?",
  "answer": "Yes for exact physical holding routes; no for article-level access in the reviewed anonymous web route. The CiNii/NII record BA65589403 explicitly lists volume 3 at Kyoto University Institute for Research in Humanities, Kyoto University Graduate School/Faculty of Letters, and the University of Tokyo Faculty of Letters Chinese Thought collection, each with a volume-specific call/location string and holding/item identifier. The public CiNii record does not expose the supplement article author, page range or body. Following the Kyoto and Tokyo OPAC links in the reviewed anonymous browser route returned HTTP 403. This is recorded only as a current anonymous-fetch boundary, not as proof that the libraries deny normal human access, on-site use, reference service or lawful reproduction. No request, login, identity transmission, payment or copy order was submitted.",
